# Netlify and Cloudflare Pages read this file: the old addresses forward permanently (301).
# Every rule is written twice. Netlify skips a rule when a file is at the old address (the page left there,
# which still forwards on other hosts) unless its status carries a "!"; Cloudflare Pages always forwards and
# drops a line it cannot read, so the plain line is the one it uses.
/bronnenscan/  /waterlichaam-bronnenanalyse/  301!
/bronnenscan/  /waterlichaam-bronnenanalyse/  301
/en/bronnenscan/  /en/waterbody-source-analysis/  301!
/en/bronnenscan/  /en/waterbody-source-analysis/  301
